v class=\"wp-block-uagb-image uagb-block-b6f7a8b9 wp-block-uagb-image--layout-default wp-block-uagb-image--effect-static wp-block-uagb-image--align-none\"><figure class=\"wp-block-uagb-image__figure\"><img srcset=\"http:\/\/localhost:8090\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Skwnz47Kl7CanzuedwDAB_7c6d9d516e2a4c72b5526d863768a078.webp ,http:\/\/localhost:8090\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Skwnz47Kl7CanzuedwDAB_7c6d9d516e2a4c72b5526d863768a078.webp 780w, http:\/\/localhost:8090\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Skwnz47Kl7CanzuedwDAB_7c6d9d516e2a4c72b5526d863768a078.webp 360w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 480px) 150px\" src=\"http:\/\/localhost:8090\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/Skwnz47Kl7CanzuedwDAB_7c6d9d516e2a4c72b5526d863768a078.webp\" alt=\"Illustration of a massage therapist working on a client lying face down.\" class=\"uag-image-1114\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" title=\"Therapeutic Massage by Butsaba\" role=\"img\"\/><\/figure><\/div>\n<!-- \/wp:uagb\/image -->\n\n<!-- wp:uagb\/advanced-heading {\"block_id\":\"c7a8b9c0\",\"classMigrate\":true,\"headingDescToggle\":false,\"headingColor\":\"var(--ast-global-color-0)\",\"blockLeftPadding\":28,\"blockBottomPadding\":100,\"blockTopPaddingTablet\":0,\"blockRightPaddingTablet\":0,\"blockLeftPaddingTablet\":0,\"blockBottomPaddingTablet\":0,\"blockTopPaddingMobile\":8,\"blockRightPaddingMobile\":0,\"blockLeftPaddingMobile\":0,\"blockBottomPaddingMobile\":0} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-advanced-heading uagb-block-c7a8b9c0\"><\/div>\n<!-- \/wp:uagb\/advanced-heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:uagb\/advanced-heading {\"block_id\":\"d8b9c0d1\",\"classMigrate\":true,\"headingDescToggle\":true,\"subHeadingColor\":\"\",\"headSpace\":8,\"subHeadSpace\":0} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-advanced-heading uagb-block-d8b9c0d1\"><h2 class=\"uagb-heading-text\">What Is Therapeutic Massage?<\/h2><p class=\"uagb-desc-text\">Therapeutic massage combines focused work with time to relax. I start with what brought you in. You can ask me to stay with one area, such as your neck and shoulders, or to work more broadly, and the plan can change as you give me feedback.<br><br>Research suggests that massage therapy may help reduce pain in some conditions and may improve certain movement-related outcomes in studied pain populations.<a href=\"https:\/\/pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\/39008297\/\">[1]<\/a><a href=\"https:\/\/pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\/27165971\/\">[2]<\/a> Studies of sports massage have found small improvements in flexibility and exercise-related muscle soreness.<a href=\"https:\/\/pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\/32426160\/\">[3]<\/a> Brief massage has been studied for short-term relaxation.<a href=\"https:\/\/pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\/32901072\/\">[4]<\/a> Regular massage was associated with improved well-being in a small four-week study of older adults.<a href=\"https:\/\/pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\/17709060\/\">[5]<\/a><br><br>Research has explored massage among people living with chronic pain, people recovering from stroke with related disability, people with cancer-related symptoms, and family caregivers.<a href=\"https:\/\/pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\/27165971\/\">[2]<\/a><a href=\"https:\/\/pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\/33919371\/\">[6]<\/a><a href=\"https:\/\/pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\/39558520\/\">[7]<\/a><a href=\"https:\/\/pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\/31003683\/\">[8]<\/a> Research has also examined massage in relation to stress, anxiety, and quality-of-life measures in specific adult groups.<a href=\"https:\/\/pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\/27901219\/\">[9]<\/a><a href=\"https:\/\/pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\/33053005\/\">[10]<\/a><a href=\"https:\/\/pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\/17709060\/\">[5]<\/a><\/p><\/div>\n<!-- \/wp:uagb\/advanced-heading --><\/div>\n<!-- \/wp:uagb\/container -->\n\n<!-- wp:uagb\/container {\"block_id\":\"e9c0d1e2\",\"bottomPaddingDesktop\":40,\"topPaddingTablet\":0,\"bottomPaddingTablet\":40,\"leftPaddingTablet\":0,\"rightPaddingTablet\":0,\"topPaddingMobile\":0,\"bottomPaddingMobile\":30,\"leftPaddingMobile\":0,\"right